On 2009-01-08, David Damerell <damerell@chiark.greenend.org.uk> wrote:
> Quoting   <pridehigh@gmail.com>:
>>"Dragonlance."  As an artifact, it won't break from jousting.
>
> Balance issues, much?

It's a lance which never breaks, instead of breaking <0.05% of the
time.  It gives a small bonus to hit, which is almost irrelevant.  It
gives a good bonus to damage against dragons only, which is nice
enough, but not why you'd go out of your way to get it.

It's an unaligned artifact.  On the one hand, it could appear on the
floor or be generated through sacrifice (and with "enough" sacrifice
will eventually be generated).  On the other hand, it affects the
number of artifacts you can generate through wishing (and carries the
difficulty of wishing for it).

It's a good enough weapon to ascend with.  So are a bunch of other
artifacts.  A knight might consider wishing for it.

Also, being an artifact, you can't two-weapon it with Excalibur/GS.

What are the balance issues?  If it had a power other than
"unbreakable lance", it could easily get problematic despite the extra
effort of setting up riding to rely on a lance, but as described?


